 "story": {
  "kicker": "Gentilly",
  "h2": "New Orleans Snowball",
  "paragraphs": [
   "The sign across the front says NEW ORLEANS SNOBALL SMOOTHEE PO-BOY and the banner under it says OPEN YEAR ROUND, which in this city is the whole argument. Sno-ball stands are a seasonal business and plenty of them board up when it cools off. This one on Elysian Fields runs ten to seven, seven days a week, in January the same as in July.",
   "It is also considerably more than a sno-ball stand. The pylon sign out by the road lists hot plates, po-boys, seafood, wings and catering, and the review photos back every bit of that up: nachos buried under jalapeños, plates of hot food, and a smoothee thick enough to hold the straw upright. The sno-balls run to the full rainbow, and the move people keep writing about is asking for condensed milk over the top."
  ]
 },
